+# Volt wheel fit and formed fenders — 2026-10-31
+
+VWF01 brings each front visual wheel inward by 50 mm in authored coordinates, or **4.4 cm at world scale**. Rear-wheel placement, wheel size, canonical handling and collision configuration retain their task-start values. VWF02 replaces the previous nearly flat arch strips with four formed painted fenders. They blend into the body and project up to **4.8 cm** at world scale, with a rolled return around each opening. Their lower feet meet the existing body edge.
+
+VWF03 closes the wheel housings. The former liners were open transverse strips; horizontal rays could pass through every sampled bay. Each bay now has a curved liner roof, opaque inboard bulkhead and end walls. A closed central undertray sits inside the lower body. The return edges and inner walls use the same sampled boundaries. These are actual opaque surfaces, with the tire aperture left open.
+
+[Matched before/after views](evidence/volt-fenders-2026-10-31/before-after.html) include frontal, quarter, close wheel, low and full-steering angles. The [front-wheel close-up](evidence/volt-fenders-2026-10-31/final-gl-seated/left-front-low.png) shows the rolled fender and dark enclosed bay. Both desktop Compatibility and desktop Mobile have nine final native views.
+
+The new actual-buffer regression passes **96/96** on procedural and prepared full/simple models. Across each run, all **120/120 wheel-bay rays** are blocked, versus **0/120** on the task-start control. Actual tire vertices are checked at five steering angles through the existing ±0.4 rad visual range and three rotation phases. They retain at least 57.4 mm authored clearance to the front inboard walls, and remain inside the liner's curved clearance envelope. The undertray is tested for vertical/lateral closure and correct seating. The accepted hood, windshield, panoramic roof and rear-glass arrays match the preceding prepared model exactly. The control fails 40/80 final checks as expected.
+
+The retained sports regression passes 104/104, including exact same-process parity for all **333 prepared meshes**. Its old front-wheel-position assertion is explicitly updated for this owner's requested inset; original axle height and longitudinal position remain checked. The focused Electric Garage-template 4/4, picture identity 5/5 and racing 23/23 checks pass. Actual App Garage/race checks pass 58/58 on Compatibility with nine captures; frame-hitch logs remain, so this is a functional check. Final visible geometry remains within the existing limits: 118,616 detailed and 37,720 simple triangles, with 3,388 separate simple shadow triangles.
+
+Three runtime files change: `electric_reference_body.gd`, `electric_reference_details.gd`, and the prepared-root constant in `electric_reference_mesh.gd`. The new mesh directory is `electric_sport_fenders_v1`; the preceding fastback directory is retained and hashed. Prepared meshes, five shadow proxies, the Electric Garage template and 52 Electric pictures are regenerated. The existing mesh-root picture identity rejects older saved Volt pictures. Only Electric's Garage template is refreshed, preserving concurrent car work; other templates may rebuild under the shared editor source guard.
+
+The initial focused test used an unsupported `PackedVector3Array.all()` call and was corrected to explicit iteration. Early low-angle views exposed a low undertray edge; it was seated inside the bumper, with a new coverage/seating check. Initial renders, failures and intermediate results remain in the evidence folder. Every engine launch uses `scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py` with an isolated offline profile. Root-certificate-store warnings remain in the Windows logs.
+
+[Commands, hashes, actual outcomes and the checked source patch](evidence/volt-fenders-2026-10-31/report.json) record delivery. Reload/rebuild, owner appearance acceptance and physical-device review remain. No device query/test, APK, owner-save/live/backend mutation, deployment, owner-process restart or main-index write was performed. Desktop views are not phone-performance measurements.
